          "detail": "rsync 3.4.1: a bare rate uses 1024 bytes/second; fractions are allowed. Single-letter K/M/G/T/P and KiB/MiB/GiB/TiB/PiB use powers of 1024; KB/MB/GB/TB/PB use powers of 1000; B means bytes. Suffix letters are case-insensitive. The size grammar also allows a trailing +1 or -1 byte offset. Rates are rounded to KiB/second granularity; a nonzero limit cannot be smaller than 1024 bytes/second. Zero disables the limit. Do not append a literal /s suffix."
